[18.35,"o","# Mission: Fix hello world greeting typos in hello.sh (parallix-adhoc-0001)\r\n\r\n## Goal\r\nCorrect the misspelled greeting emitted by `hello.sh` so that running `./hello.sh` prints exactly `H \bello, World!` followed by a newline, instead of the current `Helo, Wrld!`.\r\n\r\n## Why Now\r\n`hello.sh` is the only executable artifact in this repository and its output is the repository's sin \bgle user-visible behaviour. The current output contains two spelling errors (`Helo` instead of `Hell \bo`, `Wrld` instead of `World`), so the repository ships a visibly broken greeting. The fix is a one- \bline `printf` correction, so shipping it now removes the defect at effectively zero risk and leaves  \bthe repository in a state where any future work starts from correct baseline output.\r\n\r\n## Refinement Signals\r\n- Predicted NEL bucket: Small (0–80)\r\n- Confidence: High\r\n- Selection note: activate as-is\r\n- Main drivers: single-file change to `hello.sh`; one `printf` string literal; no build system, no d \bependencies, no existing test suite to u"]
[21.35,"o","pdate; verification gate `./scripts/verify-local.sh` is a no \b-op stub, so evidence must come from direct command output plus the changed file path.\r\n\r\n## Scope\r\n- Edit the `printf` line in `hello.sh` so the emitted text is `Hello, World!` with a trailing newlin \b\u001b[7mmissions/parallix-adhoc-0001/MISSION.md\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
